  "text": "Mercury was a Celtic god of the Continent and Britain. The Romans renamed many localized Celtic gods after him. Caesar wrote that Mercury was the god most worshiped among the Celts. He appeared often in Celtic art. Under his Roman name he stayed popular across the Celtic lands. Celtic images show him with a cock, ram, or goat. Those animals stand for virility and masculine power. Mercury was not a warrior. He was a god of commerce and prosperity. He carried a bag or purse of money. He often wore a torc, the twisted neck-piece of prestige. At times he held the caduceus, a winged double-snake staff linked to healing. He was often paired with Rosmerta, a goddess of water and healing. The pair were worshiped at Braint, in Gaul. Many local gods took his name, including Teutates, Esus, and Mercury Visucius.",
